  "id": "COMPOUND:23096 - PROTEIN:4972",
  "verbalization": "Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside) is implicated in the biological pathway leading to LAMA-84 through a series of target relationships. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by another compound, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which also targets LAMA-84. This indicates a potential chain of interaction where Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside) may influence LAMA-84 via these intermediaries. The presence of multiple pathways converging on LAMA-84 suggests a possible role for Quercetin 3-(6''-p-hydroxybenzoylgalactoside) in modulating the activity of these intermediates, potentially through direct or indirect mechanisms. The integration of these findings highlights the complexity of the biological network and underscores the importance of understanding the interplay between these compounds in determining their functional roles.",
